  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.4.0: one channel per MCP endpoint. New: LineMcpOptions.ChannelName (empty, the default channel, unless set) picks the official account whose Messaging and LIFF clients every tool and the outbox service use, through LineMcpClients; the default channel prefers a directly registered client, so a host without a factory keeps working. A channel that is not registered makes every tool answer line.not_configured, send nothing and never fall back to another account, and the sending tools refuse at proposal time. line_get_bot_info reports channelName; line_upsert_auto_reply and line_test_auto_reply take an optional channelName. No tool was renamed or removed. See https://github.com/ozakboy/Ozakboy.Line/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
